course: dictionary
lesson: 15470
title: Storybook: a book or a dream
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A storybook is a book of stories, often for children, and often with pictures. «Mum read me a storybook at bedtime.» Here storybook is a noun, a thing you can hold and open.
explain: Storybook can also be a describing word. «The village had storybook cottages with red roofs and flower gardens.» The cottages are not books. They look as pretty and perfect as the places in a fairy tale.
explain: Use the clues around the word. If the sentence mentions pages, shelves or pictures, storybook is the book. If it talks about a place, a day or an ending, storybook describes it. «The wedding was a storybook day, with sunshine and music.»
fact: A storybook is a book of stories for children, often with pictures.
fact: As an adjective, storybook means perfect or magical, like something from a fairy tale.
fact: «A storybook ending» means an ending that is happy and perfect.
fact: A good check is to swap in the words «like in a fairy tale»: if the sentence still makes sense, storybook is being used as a describing word.
exercise: «She picked a storybook from the shelf and sat down to read.» What is a storybook here? | A kind of shelf | A long, sad poem | A quiet place to sit | *A book of stories for children
exercise: «The castle with its towers and gardens was storybook perfect.» What does storybook mean here? | *Perfect and magical, like a fairy tale | Full of noisy visitors | Made of wood and very old | Covered in snow
exercise: Which word in this sentence means a book of stories? «My favourite storybook has talking animals on every page.» | *storybook | page | favourite | talking
test: «The little house at the end of the lane looked like a storybook cottage.» What does storybook mean here? | *Pretty and magical, like a fairy tale | A cottage that sells books | Made only of stone | Dark and empty
test: «Dad bought me a storybook with pictures of dragons.» What is a storybook in this sentence? | A school bag | A map of the forest | A tall wooden shelf | *A book of stories with pictures
exam: «The ending was storybook perfect, and everyone lived happily ever after.» What does storybook suggest? | *Perfect and happy, like a fairy tale | Rushed and messy | Written in a foreign language | Sad and lonely
